<div class="page-wrap"><div class="home-layout"><div class="calc-section-wrap" style="width:100%;">
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href="mailto:support@solvecalc.net">support@solvecalc.net</a>. It is the same inbox that handles the main site, so mentioning that you are writing about the GitHub Pages build gets your message to the right place faster.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Reporting a Wrong Result</h2>
    <p>Three details make a report actionable: the exact expression you entered, what the screen showed, and what you expected instead. Add the browser you were using and a problem can usually be reproduced immediately. Without them it rarely can.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Issues and Pull Requests</h2>
    <p>Because this build is open source, a GitHub issue is often faster than an email for anything code related. Open one at <a href="https://github.com/solvecalc/solvecalc.github.io/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/solvecalc/solvecalc.github.io</a>, and include the page URL.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Suggesting a Tool</h2>
    <p>Tell me the calculation you keep doing by hand and which year group it belongs to. Requests that arrive more than once tend to get built first.</p>
  </section>
